<div id="recipe-82917-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82917-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82917"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat your oven to 375 &deg;F (191 &deg;C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Into a bowl, place harissa, honey, olive oil, lemon juice, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper. Whisk until fully combined. Taste for seasoning and add more if necessary. Set it aside.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person making the harissa sauce for the salmon." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Salmon-with-harissa-paste.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Pat-dry the salmon on both sides using a few sheets of parchment paper. Transfer it to the prepared baking sheet.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Spread the harissa mixture evenly on the salmon, ensuring that all the top and sides are fully covered. There is no need to spread harissa at the bottom. Top it off with a few slices of lemon.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Photos showing the salmon being prepared for baking." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Harissa-fish.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Bake in the preheated oven for 12-14 minutes or until your salmon registers between 125 to 135 &deg;F.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Photos showing harissa salmon before and after it is baked." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/how-to-make-salmon-spicy.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82917-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Garnish with parsley and serve it with lemon slices/wedges on the side.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-82917-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Salmon</strong>: I prefer using wild Alaskan salmon (such as Sockeye Salmon or King Salmon) in most of my salmon recipes, and this one is no exception. However, you can use any salmon you can get your hands on. If it is thawed, be sure to fully thaw it before spreading it with harissa. Also, keep in mind that the baking time could change based on the thickness of your salmon.</li>
<li><strong>A Whole filet or slices?</strong> Both would work. I usually shop for salmon in Costco, and they sell it as a filet. However, sliced salmon can also be used.&nbsp;</li>
<li><strong>Skin on or off:&nbsp;</strong>Both would work.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:&nbsp;</strong>While this dish tastes best fresh out of the oven leftovers can be kept in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 2 days.</li>
</ul></div></div>
